      "description": "Most people miss out on things they would have got. Not because they were not good enough, but because nobody sent them the link.\n\nFEJA is where the link lives.\n\nInternships, scholarships, exchanges, workshops and more, for young people, collected in one feed and filtered to what you can actually get.\n\n\nWHAT YOU CAN DO\n\nBrowse. One card per listing, with who is running it, where it is, and how long is left before it closes.\n\nMatched to you from the start. Your age and your country are applied to the feed by default, so what you cannot enter is out of the way before you start scrolling. Switch it off in one tap when you want to see everything.\n\nNarrow it further. Filter by type, topic, cost, format and region, or show only what is still open. Sort by deadline when time is short.\n\nQuick Match. One listing at a time. Swipe right to save it, left to skip.\n\nCheck the small print first. Age limits, residency rules and requirements sit at the top of a listing, above the description, so you know in seconds whether to read on.\n\nSave what you like. Everything you keep sits in one place, ready when you are.\n\nApply. One tap opens the organiser's own site, where you apply to them directly.\n\n\nWHERE THESE COME FROM\n\nWe go and find them. EU institutions, national parliaments, government funding bodies, university foundations, charities, and the small outfits that quietly run good programmes and never get found. Every listing links straight to whoever runs it.\n\nFEJA is independent. We are not affiliated with, endorsed by or partnered with any organisation we list, and nobody pays us to be listed.\n\n\nWHAT IT COSTS\n\nNothing. FEJA is free. No subscription, nothing to buy inside the app, and we never ask for payment details.\n\n\nWHAT WE DO NOT DO\n\nNo ads. No tracking you across other apps. No selling your information. No third-party analytics. FEJA never reads your location, your country is something you type in. When you tap Apply you leave FEJA, and we send the organiser nothing about you.\n\n\nWHO IT IS FOR\n\nYou have to be 16 or over to have an account. Most of what is here suits 16 to 30: school students, university students, apprentices, school leavers, anyone on a gap year, and anyone in a first job who still wants the trip, the grant, or the room where the decision gets made.\n\n\nONE HONEST THING\n\nFEJA is not the provider. We do not run admissions and we do not decide who gets in. Deadlines move and details change, so always confirm on the organiser's own site before you rely on it. Spot something wrong and we will fix it.\n\n\nPrivacy Policy: https://ofeja.com/privacy\nTerms of Service: https://ofeja.com/terms\nTerms of Use (EULA): https://www.apple.com/legal/internet-services/itunes/dev/stdeula/\nSupport: https://ofeja.com/support",
